    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's an interesting distinction. When you say the Madonna piece reflects an \"ordered religious worldview\" while the mask is \"visceral\" and \"culturally specific,\" is there a way to talk about the intellectual depth of the mask without making it sound like it's just based on emotion or ritual? \n\nI don't want the essay to imply that the European work is \"thinking\" art while the African work is just \"feeling\" art. How would a historian bridge that gap in terms of complexity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
